### Suggested .gitignore entries

Add the following to your repo `.gitignore` to avoid committing the venv and other common unwanted files:

```gitignore
# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/

# Python cache and compiled files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class


# Installer logs
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt



# Logs and temporary files
*.log
tmp/
*.tmp

# Optional: lock files or local config
# requirements.txt should be committed; local lock files can be ignored if you prefer
# Pipenv
Pipfile.lock

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/


